#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using and Customizing Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introdución"

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many &kde; applications allow you to configure keyboard shortcuts. To open "
"the standard keyboard shortcuts configuration panel, go to "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the Configure Shortcuts window, you will see a list of all the hotkeys "
"available in the current application. You can use the search box at the top "
"to search for the shortcut you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: config.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Customize Shortcuts Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: config.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Customize Shortcuts window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Searching for shortcuts with <userinput>file</userinput> in <ulink url="
"\"http://kde.org/applications/system/dolphin/\">&dolphin;</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing a Hotkey"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change a hotkey, first click on the name of a shortcut you want to "
"change. You will see a radio group where you can choose whether to set the "
"hotkey to its default value, or select a new hotkey for the selected action. "
"To set a new hotkey, choose <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> and click on the "
"button next to it. Then just type the hotkey you would like to use, and your "
"changes will be saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: config.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting a Hotkey"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: config.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Customize Shortcuts window demonstrating how to set a hotkey."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resetting Hotkeys"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a button at the bottom of the window, called <guibutton>Reset to "
"Defaults</guibutton>. Clicking on this button will reset all your custom "
"shortcuts to their default values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also reset an individual hotkey to its default value by selecting "
"it, and choosing the <guilabel>Default</guilabel> radio button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing a Hotkey"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a hotkey, select it from the list, then click the remove icon (a "
"black arrow with a cross) to the right of the button that allows you to "
"select a shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Working with Schemes</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Schemes are keyboard shortcuts configuration profiles, so you can create "
"several profiles with different hotkeys and switch between these profiles "
"easily."
msgstr ""

